From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lef <me@lefteros.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:00:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zuma-husky: describe the pack
 EEPROM on hsi2c_9

The Pixel 8 Pro's battery pack has an EEPROM on USI9 / hsi2c_9: stock
has it as "at,24c08" at 0x50 on a 400 kHz bus. Its byte 0x17 is the
battery ID that Google's driver matches against the fuel gauge models
(0 the default model, 1 ATL, 2 COS, 3 LSN, 170 Google's dummy), and
which pack the phone has is what decides the right model. The rest of
the EEPROM holds the pack's part number, dates and history, so the node
is read-only.

Mainline's at24 driver wants "atmel,24c08", not stock's alias. The bus
and USI9 stay disabled in the board file, like hsi2c_11; a bring-up
overlay enables them. Nothing feeds the ID to the gauge yet.

Tested on a Pixel 8 Pro (slot B, release 7.3.0-rc6-omamobile-push1-
g7975b84a8017: Brett's c6 tree with #163 and the four commits of this
series, as the branch husky-pack-eeprom-booted). A bring-up overlay
enabled cmu_peric1, the sysreg, USI9 and hsi2c_9. The log shows

  at24 0-0050: 1024 byte 24c08 EEPROM, read-only

and a one-byte read of offset 0x17 returned 1, the ATL pack.

Signed-off-by: Lef <me@lefteros.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts     | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
index 7a520b985..f9d30456a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
@@ -311,3 +311,22 @@ gpio {
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * The battery pack's EEPROM on USI9 / hsi2c_9 (stock: "at,24c08" at 0x50 on
+ * a 400 kHz bus, in the pack and powered by it). Byte 0x17 is the battery ID
+ * that Google's driver matches against the gauge models; the rest is the
+ * pack's part number, dates and history, so it is read-only here. The bus
+ * and USI9 stay disabled; a bring-up overlay enables them. Nothing reads the
+ * ID into the gauge yet.
+ */
+&hsi2c_9 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+
+	eeprom@50 {
+		compatible = "atmel,24c08";
+		reg = <0x50>;
+		pagesize = <16>;
+		read-only;
+	};
+};
